The occupancy for the STAR PMD is defined as the ratio of total number of cells hit to the total number of cells. The occupancy is reflective of the granularity of the detector and for a fixed granularity the particle density falling on the detector. The detector configuration is designed to keep the occupancy to a lower level, so that efficiency of particle identification and counting is good. Fig. 3.21 shows the

